{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:11.201Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Pytorch image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Pytorch?\n\nPytorch is an open source machine learning framework that accelerates the path from research prototyping to production deployment.\n\nSee: [PyTorch](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PyTorch).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `2`\n- `2-cm2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Pytorch version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a PyTorch app with package dependencies\n\nIf your PyTorch app has a requirements.txt defining your app's dependencies, you can install the dependencies before running your app.\n\n    docker run -it --rm \\\n    --name pytorch \\\n    -v /path/to/app:/app \\\n    mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch:2 \\\n    sh -c \"pip install -r requirements.txt && python my-script.py\"\n\nThe default container startup command is `python`.\n\n### Run a single Pytorch script\n\nFor many simple, single file projects, you may just run a Pytorch script (named my-script.py in the example below) by using the Mariner based Pytorch docker image directly. The default work directory for the PyTorch image is /app. You can mount a folder from your host here that includes your PyTorch script, and run it normally using the python command.\n    \n    docker run -it --rm --name running-pytorch \\\n    -v /path/to/app:/app mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch:2 \\\n    python my-script.py\n\n### Run the container to get Pytorch version\n\nYou can run a single docker command to print the pytorch version installed in the image:\n\n    docker run -it --rm \\\n    mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch:2 \\\n    python -c \"import torch; print(torch.__version__)\" \n\n### Run Pytorch repl environment\n\nYou may want to simply run the Python interactive shell that comes with Pytorch image by launching it when the container starts. In such case, you can run Python REPL with a new pytorch enviroment activated by using the Mariner based Pytorch docker image directly. The following command will launch the virtual environment that Pytorch comes with:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch:2\n\n### Launch Mariner shell\n\nThe Pytorch image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to launch Mariner shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/pytorch:2 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:53:18.1408499+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"228K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"2.0-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:ea047ed18056dcb02652e1c7d4f204ae13bd653593cc490aea88a1986067ceea","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:42:42.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.0","digest":"sha256:ea047ed18056dcb02652e1c7d4f204ae13bd653593cc490aea88a1986067ceea","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:42:32.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:ea047ed18056dcb02652e1c7d4f204ae13bd653593cc490aea88a1986067ceea","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:42:24.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2","digest":"sha256:ea047ed18056dcb02652e1c7d4f204ae13bd653593cc490aea88a1986067ceea","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:42:12.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"2.0.0-15-cm2.0.20260311-arm64","digest":"sha256:41a892662e0a5850b3b0e6bb6a20e0d1a49f7c700fa63246a932d624539dcc02","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:42:08.0000000+00:00","size":5446,"platforms":["linux/arm